## 3. Step-by-Step Vercel Deployment Instructions

### Step 1: Import Project to Vercel
1. Log in to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com).
2. Click **"Add New..."** &rarr; **"Project"**.
3. Select your GitHub repository: **`MD-Kayesur/family-together-frontend`**.

### Step 2: Configure Project Settings
- **Framework Preset:** `Next.js` (automatically detected)
- **Root Directory:** `./` (default)
- **Build Command:** `next build` (or `npm run build`)
- **Output Directory:** `.next` (automatically managed)

### Step 3: Set Required Environment Variables
In the **Environment Variables** section on Vercel, add:

| Key | Example Value | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | `https://your-backend.railway.app` | The publicly accessible URL of your deployed NestJS backend API |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> If `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` is omitted, the frontend defaults to `http://localhost:8000`, which will not be accessible to users in production. Be sure to deploy your backend or point this variable to your live backend server.

### Step 4: Click "Deploy"
Vercel will clone the repository, run `npm run build`, and assign your live production URL (e.g. `https://family-together-frontend.vercel.app`).
